# .github/scripts Context

## Purpose
- Stores helper payloads/config files consumed directly by GitHub workflow steps.
- These files support automation behavior but are not app runtime code.

## Current Usage
- `append-firebase-env.json` is used by deploy workflow SSM commands to append Firebase-related environment settings on EC2.

## Conventions
- Keep payload files deterministic and environment-safe.
- Preserve compatibility with AWS SSM `send-command` expectations (quoting/escaping is critical).
- Prefer additive, explicit commands over opaque command chains.
- Keep file naming descriptive of the workflow step they support.

## Agent Guidance
- Validate any path/name changes against references in `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`.
- Do not move these helpers to repository root scripts unless workflow references are updated.
- Never introduce plaintext secrets into tracked helper payloads.

## Distinction From Root scripts/
- `.github/scripts/` is workflow-local helper data/config.
- `scripts/` at repository root contains broader operational scripts and may be invoked by workflows.
